# Tylicious Grillz

A full-stack food ordering and restaurant storefront built with Next.js, React, and TypeScript.

## Live Website

https://www.tyliciousgrillz.com/

## Project Overview

I built Tylicious Grillz to provide customers with an interactive online food ordering experience. The project combines a responsive storefront with configurable menu items, basket management, and an online checkout flow.

## Tech Stack

- Next.js
- React
- TypeScript
- GSAP
- Supabase
- Stripe

## Key Features

- Browse menu items and product categories.
- Configure meals using available product options.
- Add items to the basket and adjust quantities.
- Remove items and review selected options.
- View confirmation when adding items to the basket.
- Complete online checkout using Stripe.
- Store product and order-related data using Supabase.

## Checkout Implementation

Stripe checkout is implemented and has been tested end to end. The checkout flow integrates with the application's ordering process.

## My Contribution

I built the project from scratch, working across the frontend experience, application logic, database integration, and payment checkout flow.

## Engineering Focus

This project demonstrates my practical experience with React and Next.js application development, TypeScript, interactive UI behaviour, data integration, and payment workflows.

## Repository

